From 49f17a1e44082fe8c509172cd67075edb2b56798 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 05:56:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gitattributes: evidence receipt files are byte-exact (-text)

Series replay onto 9e0e22059 differed from arifi/main only in eight build-log receipts under
r46b-b7b-loader-evidence/ and r46b-b7c-evidence/ (1584 lines swapped: line-ending conversion).
Marking the evidence trees -text and renormalizing makes the committed blobs byte-exact.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - HQ seat-58 series maintenance
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - repository hygiene
Lane: lane-233
---
 .gitattributes | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitattributes b/.gitattributes
index 695b3ec9c..7fe7c6e34 100644
--- a/.gitattributes
+++ b/.gitattributes
@@ -18,3 +18,6 @@ patches/** -text diff
 # on Linux and macOS with an unhelpful 'bad interpreter' error, and Git for Windows defaults
 # core.autocrlf=true - so pin them to LF regardless of the cloner's settings.
 .githooks/** text eol=lf
+
+# HQ seat-58 2026-09-14: raw evidence receipts are byte-exact records; never eol-convert them (series replay parity)
+r46b-*-evidence/** -text
